OperationsWe can perform a variety of operations on the Matrix Data Structure. Some of the most common operations are: 1. Access Elements of Matrix Like one-dimensional arrays, matrices can be accessed randomly by using their indices to access the individual elements. A cell has two indices, one for its row number, and the other for its column number. We can use arr[i][j] to access the element which is at the ith row and jth column of the matrix.
            C++

    #include <iostream>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

int main()
{
    // Initializing a 2-D vector with values
    vector<vector<int>> arr = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}, {7, 8, 9}};

    // Accessing elements of 2-D vector
    cout << "First element of first row: " << arr[0][0] << "\n";
    cout << "Third element of second row: " << arr[1][2] << "\n";
    cout << "Second element of third row: " << arr[2][1] << "\n";

    return 0;
}


